    "result_text": "The build is green: **Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0** and **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `membershipNumber` as a derived field, `'<customerCode>-M<YY>'` where YY is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`).\n\nSince `membershipNumber` is purely computed from an owner's own fields \u2014 exactly like the existing `displayName` and `initials` derived fields \u2014 I added it at the DTO mapping layer rather than storing it on the entity:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema (the `OwnerDto` is code-generated from this spec at build time).\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression that computes it:\n   ```java\n   owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" + String.format(\"%02d\", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100)\n   ```\n   The `%02d` zero-pads the two-digit year (so year 2007 \u2192 `07`, 2026 \u2192 `26`).\n\nBoth inputs are guaranteed non-null on a created owner: `AssignCustomerCode` sets `customerCode` before save, and `BuildOwner` defaults `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when absent. The `AcceptanceTest.coreMembershipNumberFormat` test passes.",
